# The generation state. `.hashes/` is committed: it is one hash per generated
# path (one file per model package), and the only thing that lets `gen` tell "this file is exactly what I wrote" from
# "somebody edited this" on a machine that did not generate it. Everything else here (the
# skip key) describes one machine's last run and is not.
#
# The glob form matters: `.gen-state/` (a directory) would stop git descending, and the
# negation below could never take effect.
.gen-state/*
!.gen-state/.hashes/
